Step 1: Write down the formula for the circumference of a circle.

$$
\begin{array}{ll}
 C  {= \pi \times d}
 \end{array}
$$

Or you can use $C = \pi \times 2r$.

Step 2: The question tells us that the radius of the circle is 2 cm. So the diameter is 4 cm. Substitute 4 for the $d$ in the formula. Also substitute 3.14 for $\pi$.

$$
\begin{array}{ll}
 C & {= \pi \times d} \\
 & {= 3.14 \times 4} \\
 \end{array}
$$

As you can see, if you used $C = \pi \times 2r$, you would also get $3.14 \times 4$.

Step 3: Calculate the circumference of the circle. Remember to show the correct units in your answer.

$$
\begin{array}{ll}
 C & {= \pi \times d}\\
 &{= 3.14 \times 4}\\
 &{= \text{12.56 cm}}
 \end{array}
$$

The circumference of the circle is 12.56 cm.

